{"id": "1238", "name": "Voriconazole", "slug": "voriconazole-1238", "monograph_link": "https://medex.com.bd/attachments/O6QLXQaKIzGSfWVfrkuCTxko9Myz5t/voriconazole-prescribing-information", "drug_class": "Other Antifungal preparations", "indication": "Scedosporiosis and fusariosis", "indication_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\"><div class=\"min-str-block\"><div class=\"min-str mb-5\" style=\"display: none;\">Voriconazole is an azole antifungal medicine. It is indicated for use in patients 12 years of age and older in the treatment of following fungal infections-<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Invasive aspergillosis</li>\n<li>Candidemia (nonneutropenic) and disseminated candidiasis in skin, abdomen, kidney, bladder wall and wounds</li> <span class=\"min-str-toggle tx-green tx-bold\" style=\"cursor:pointer;font-style:italic;\">... Read more</span></ul></div><div class=\"full-str\">Voriconazole is an azole antifungal medicine. It is indicated for use in patients 12 years of age and older in the treatment of following fungal infections-<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Invasive aspergillosis</li>\n<li>Candidemia (nonneutropenic) and disseminated candidiasis in skin, abdomen, kidney, bladder wall and wounds</li>\n<li>Esophageal candidiasis</li>\n<li>Serious infections caused by Scedosporium apiospermum and Fusarium Species including Fusarium solani</li>\n<li>Patients intolerant of, or refractory to other therapy.</li>\n</ul></div></div></div>", "therapeutic_class_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Other Antifungal preparations</div>", "pharmacology_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Voriconazole is a triazole antifungal medication used to treat serious fungal infections. Voriconazole binds and inhibits ergosterol synthesis by inhibiting CYP450-dependent 14-alpha sterol demethylase. The inhibition of 14-alpha sterol demethylase results in a depletion of ergosterol in fungal cell membrane.</div>", "dosage_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Oral-<br>Voriconazole tablet and powder for suspension are to be taken at least one hour before or one hour following a meal<br>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>At or over 40 kg body weight</strong>: Loading dose regimen is 400 mg or 10 ml every 12 hours (for the first 24 hours) and maintenance dose (after first 24 hours) is 200 mg or 5 ml twice daily.</li>\n<li><strong>Below 40 Kg body weight</strong>: Loading dose regimen is 200 mg or 5 ml every 12 hours (for the first 24 hours) and maintenance dose (after first 24 hours) is 100 mg or 2.5 ml twice daily. Or, as directed by the registered physician.</li>\n</ul>\n<br>Injection-<br>Invasive Aspergillosisd :<br>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Loading dose</strong>: 6 mg/kg 12 hourly for the first 24 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance Dose</strong>: 4 mg/kg 12 hourly.</li>\n</ul>\nCandidemia in nonneutropenic patients and other deep tissue Candida infections:<br>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Loading dose</strong>: 6 mg/kg 12 hourly for the first 24 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance Dose</strong>: 3-4 mg/kg 12 hourly.</li>\n</ul>\nScedosporiosis and Fusariosis:<br>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Loading dose</strong>: 6 mg/kg 12 hourly for the first 24 hours.</li>\n<li><strong>Maintenance Dose</strong>: 4 mg/kg 12 hourly.</li>\n</ul></div>", "administration_description": "", "interaction_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\"><ul>\n<li>CYP3A4, CYP2C9 and CYP2C19 inhibitors and inducers: Adjust Voriconazole dosage and monitor for adverse reactions or lack of efficacy</li>\n<li>Voriconazole may increase the concentrations and activity of drugs that are CYP3A4, CYP2C9 and CYP2C19 substrates. Reduce doses of these other drugs and monitor for adverse reactions</li>\n<li>Increase maintenance oral and intravenous dosage of Voriconazole with co-administration of Phenytoin or Efavirenz</li>\n</ul></div>", "contraindications_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Known hypersensitivity to Voriconazole or any other components of this drug-<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Co-administration with terfenadine, astemizole, cisapride, pimozide or quinidine, sirolimus due to risk of serious adverse reactions</li>\n<li>Co-administration with rifampin, carbamazepine, long-acting barbiturates, efavirenz, ritonavir, rifabutin, ergot alkaloids and St. John's Wort due to risk of loss of efficacy</li>\n</ul></div>", "side_effects_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">The most common side effects are abdominal pain, anemia, blurred vision, headache, chest pain, nausea and diarrhea.</div>", "pregnancy_and_lactation_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant woman. It should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus.</div>", "precautions_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Long term exposure (treatment or prophylaxis) greater than 180 days requires careful assessment of the benefit-risk balance. Squamous cell carcinoma of the skin (SCC) has been reported in relation with long-term voriconazole treatment.</div>", "pediatric_usage_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">The efficacy to the children under 12 years of age is not established.</div>", "overdose_effects_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">There is no data found about overdose of Voriconazole.</div>", "duration_of_treatment_description": "", "reconstitution_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\"><strong>Reconstitution Instructions of suspension</strong>: Shake the bottle well before adding water to loosen the powder. Add 25 ml of boiled and cooled water to the bottle (5 spoons of a provided spoon). Shake the closed bottle vigorously until powder mixed completely with the water. Store reconstituted suspension between 15°-30° C. Discard suspension 14 days after reconstitution.</div>", "storage_conditions_description": "<div class=\"ac-body\">Keep out of reach of children. Store in a dry place, below 25°C temperature and protected from light. Store Voriconazole powder for suspension between 2° to 8°C temperature.</div>", "brands": [{"id": "30949", "name": "Candicon", "slug": "candicontablet200-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "200 mg", "manufacturer": "Popular Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 130.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 130.00,(8's pack: ৳ 1,040.00),"}, {"id": "32657", "name": "Candicon", "slug": "candicontablet100-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "100 mg", "manufacturer": "Popular Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 70.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 70.00,(10's pack: ৳ 700.00),"}, {"id": "29556", "name": "Canvo", "slug": "canvotablet200-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "200 mg", "manufacturer": "Everest Pharmaceuticals Ltd.", "price": "৳ 120.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 120.00,(6's pack: ৳ 720.00),"}, {"id": "29539", "name": "Caspa", "slug": "caspapowder-for-suspension200-mg5-ml", "dosage_form": "Powder for Suspension", "strength": "200 mg/5 ml", "manufacturer": "Aristopharma Ltd.", "price": "৳ 1,000.00", "package_container": "40 ml bottle: ৳ 1,000.00"}, {"id": "29538", "name": "Caspa", "slug": "caspatablet50-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "50 mg", "manufacturer": "Aristopharma Ltd.", "price": "৳ 50.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 50.00,(12's pack: ৳ 600.00),"}, {"id": "29537", "name": "Caspa", "slug": "caspatablet200-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "200 mg", "manufacturer": "Aristopharma Ltd.", "price": "৳ 120.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 120.00,(10's pack: ৳ 1,200.00),"}, {"id": "30886", "name": "Elazol", "slug": "elazoltablet200-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "200 mg", "manufacturer": "Renata Limited", "price": "৳ 120.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 120.00,(8's pack: ৳ 960.00),"}, {"id": "30869", "name": "Elazol", "slug": "elazoltablet50-mg", "dosage_form": "Tablet", "strength": "50 mg", "manufacturer": "Renata Limited", "price": "৳ 50.00", "package_container": "Unit Price: ৳ 50.00,(8's pack: ৳ 400.00),"}, {"id": "31543", "name": "Progil", "slug": "progilpowder-for-suspension200-mg5-m